1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,941
Every developer knows the frustration of staring at a multi-frame Python traceback.

2
00:00:04,941 --> 00:00:16,789
You spend hours tracing root causes across nested call stacks, manually formulating fixes, and hoping a chatbot's suggestion doesn't break syntax or introduce silent regressions into production code.

3
00:00:16,789 --> 00:00:27,265
This is Sunny-DevFix: an autonomous, verifiable code repair assistant built for the Nebius and NVIDIA Global AI Hackathon under the Coding and Agentic Engineering track.

4
00:00:27,265 --> 00:00:42,761
Sunny-DevFix transforms Python debugging into an accountable engineering workflow, pairing NVIDIA Nemotron reasoning on Nebius Token Factory with deterministic AST guardrails, cryptographic human approval gates, and disposable container verification.

5
00:00:42,761 --> 00:00:47,630
Inside the workspace, we paste defective source code and the runtime traceback.

6
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:56,567
Notice our Live Code Guardian: as you type, it continuously parses AST structures locally without executing untrusted code or making cloud calls.

7
00:00:56,567 --> 00:01:05,627
In this billing example, it immediately pinpoints line 3 and flags that tx was referenced instead of tax, giving developers instant local feedback.

8
00:01:05,627 --> 00:01:11,729
When we trigger the agentic repair, Sunny-DevFix activates its 6-stage lifecycle orchestrator.

9
00:01:11,729 --> 00:01:20,039
It maps the deepest call frame, bounds context, and prepares the structured request for NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory.

10
00:01:20,039 --> 00:01:31,010
While live cloud inference requires operator key authorization, the assistant operates seamlessly using local AST guardrails, ensuring verifiable, zero-crash evaluation.

11
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:36,366
Before anything touches disk, Sunny-DevFix enforces a mandatory human approval barrier.

12
00:01:36,366 --> 00:01:45,476
The assistant compiles the proposed code, verifies its AST syntax, and displays an interactive side-by-side code viewer with a colored unified diff.

13
00:01:45,476 --> 00:01:50,462
A single-use cryptographic approval token bound to the exact file hash is issued.

14
00:01:50,462 --> 00:01:55,079
Only when the operator explicitly approves is the patch atomically applied.

15
00:01:55,079 --> 00:02:03,334
For optional verification evidence, twin reproductions run in disposable Docker containers with zero network access and read-only filesystems.

16
00:02:03,334 --> 00:02:07,578
The scorecard confirms whether reproduction passed with zero regressions.

17
00:02:07,578 --> 00:02:16,298
And if an unexpected edge case is observed, a single click on Instant Rollback uses a one-time token to immediately restore the exact pre-patch bytes.

18
00:02:16,298 --> 00:02:21,134
Under the hood, Sunny-DevFix is engineered with zero compromise on quality.

19
00:02:21,134 --> 00:02:31,838
It is backed by 80 automated tests, 9 adversarial security suites covering prompt injection and path traversal, and a median benchmark latency under 0.2 milliseconds.

20
00:02:31,838 --> 00:02:37,770
If offline, it seamlessly falls back to its deterministic AST engine without missing a beat.

21
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:43,737
Sunny-DevFix brings transparency, safety, and verifiable evidence to agentic AI engineering.

22
00:02:43,737 --> 00:02:52,559
The complete MIT-licensed source code, judge-accessible standalone test build, and full technical documentation are available on GitHub.

23
00:02:52,559 --> 00:02:54,051
Thank you for watching!
